NOTE on the existing post-apply flush
------------------------------------
The current `mm->flush(&memo_err)` at cmd_commit.cpp:440 is deliberately LEFT IN PLACE.
After this patch it is a cheap near-no-op (the store was just synced) but it still
covers any memo write that occurs during apply_one_recno, and removing it would widen
the diff into the error-handling path for no correctness gain. Removal can be
considered separately once the ordering is proven.
